{
  "title": "42: al-Shooraa الشورى",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nحٰمٓ‏(1)\nHAA-MEEM.\nHa. Mim. (H. M.)\nعٓسٓقٓ‏(2)\nA’AASAAQAA.\nAin. Seen. Qaf. (Y. S. Q.)\nكَذٰلِكَ يُوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْكَ وَاِلَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَۙ اللّٰهُ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(3)\nKAZAALEKA YOOHEAA ELAYKA WA ELAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEKA LAAHO A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nThus doth reveal unto thee as (did He) unto those before thee, God, the Almighty, The All Wise.\nلَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَلِىُّ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(4)\nLAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ WA HOWA A’LIYYUL A’ZEEM.\nHis is whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth, and He is the Highest, the Greatest.\nتَكَادُ السَّمٰوٰتُ يَتَفَطَّرْنَ مِنْ فَوْقِهِنَّ‌ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يُسَبِّحُوْنَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَيَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ لِمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(5)\nTAKAADO AS-SAMAAWAATU YATAFATTARNA MIN FAWQEHENNA WAL MALAAA-EKATO YUSABBEHOONA BE-HAMDE RABBEHIM WAYASTAGHFEROONA LEMAN-Y FIL ARZ ALAA INNAL LAAHA HOWA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nNigh it is (that) the heavens cleave asunder from above (for the very awe of His glory), while the angels are (there) celebrating the praise of their Lord and seeking forgiveness for those in the earth; Be it known that verily, God, He (alone) is the Oft- Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ اللّٰهُ حَفِيْظٌ عَلَيْهِمْ‌ۖ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِوَكِيْلٍ‏(6)\nWAL LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONEHI AAWLEEAAAA LAAHO HAFEEZUN A’LAYHIM WA MAA ANTA A’LAYHIM BEWAKEELIN.\nAnd those who take aught besides God as their guardians, God watcheth over them, and thou art not over them a guardian.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ قُرْاٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا لِّتُنْذِرَ اُمَّ الْقُرٰى وَمَنْ حَوْلَهَا وَتُنْذِرَ يَوْمَ الْجَمْعِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ‌ؕ فَرِيْقٌ فِى الْجَنَّةِ وَفَرِيْقٌ فِى السَّعِيْرِ‏(7)\nWA KAZAALEKA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA QURAANAN A’RABIYYAL LLETUNZERA AUMMA KORAA WA MAN HAWLAHAA WATUNZERA YAWMA AL-JAME’E LAA RAYBA FEEH FAREEQUM FIL JANNAH WA FAREEQUM FIL SA-E’ER.\nAnd thus have We revealed unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) an Arabic Qur’an, that thou mayest warn the Mother City (Mecca) and those around it, and (that) thou warn of the Day of Gathering together (the Resurrection), wherein (there) is no doubt; (when) a party shall be in the garden (of Paradise) and a party (shall be) in the burning (Hell) fire.\nوَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَجَعَلَهُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّلٰكِنْ يُّدْخِلُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ فِىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ؕ وَالظّٰلِمُوْنَ مَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(8)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAJAA’ALAHUM UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN LAAKIL YUDKHELO MAN YASHAAA-O FEE RAHMATEH WA ZAALEMOON MAA LAHUM MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nAnd had God (so) pleased certainly would He have made them a single people, but admitteth He whosoever He willeth into His mercy; and the unjust, for them shall not be any guardian or a helper.\nاَمِ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ‌ۚ فَاللّٰهُ هُوَ الْوَلِىُّ وَهُوَ يُحْىِ الْمَوْتٰى وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(9)\nAMIL ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONEHI AAWLEEAAAA FAL-LAAHO HOWA AL-WALEAAAU WA HOWA LAAHUL MAWTAA WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nOr have they taken besides Him, guardians? But God, He is the Guardian, and He giveth life unto the dead, and He is, over all things powerful.\nوَمَا اخْتَلَفْتُمْ فِيْهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ فَحُكْمُهٗۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبِّىْ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُۖ وَاِلَيْهِ اُنِيْبُ‏(10)\nWA MAA AKHTALAFTUM FEEHE MIN SHAY-IN FAHUKMUH ELAL LAAHE ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBEE A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTU WA ELAYHE AUNEEBU.\nAnd in whatever thing ye differ, its decision is unto God; (for) that is your God my Lord, on Him rely I, and unto Him (alone) do I (always) turn.\nفَاطِرُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِكُمْ اَزْوَاجًا وَّ مِنَ الْاَنْعَامِ اَزْوَاجًا‌ ۚ يَذْرَؤُكُمْ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهٖ شَىْءٌ ‌ۚ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(11)\nFAATERU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ JA-A’LA LAKUM MIN ANFOSEKUM AZWAAJANW WA MENAL AL-AANA’AAME AZWAAJANW YAZRAUKUM FEEHE LAYSA KAMESLEH SHAY-UN WA HOWA SAMEE-U’L AL-BASEERU.\nThe Originator of the heavens and the earth; He made for you from among your (own) selves pairs, and of the cattle (too) pairs, thereby He multiplieth you; Nothing whatsoever (is there) like the like of Him; and He (alone) is the All-Hearing and the All-Seeing.\nلَهٗ مَقَالِيْدُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ۚ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(12)\nLAHU MAQAALEEDU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAQDER INNAHU BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nHis are the treasures of the heavens and the earth; amplifieth He the sustenance unto whomsoever He willeth and straiteneth; Verily He knoweth all things.\nشَرَعَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ الدِّيْنِ مَا وَصّٰى بِهٖ نُوْحًا وَّالَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ وَمَا وَصَّيْنَا بِهٖۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَمُوْسٰى وَعِيْسٰٓى اَنْ اَقِيْمُوا الدِّيْنَ وَ لَا تَتَفَرَّقُوْا فِيْهِ‌ؕ كَبُرَ عَلَى الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ مَا تَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلَيْهِ‌ ؕ اَللّٰهُ يَجْتَبِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ مَنْ يُّنِيْبُ‏(13)\nSHARAA’A LAKUM MENAL DEENE MAA WASSAA BEHI ARSALNAA WWAALLAZEAA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA WA MAA WASSAYNAA BEHI IBRAAHEEMA WA MOOSAA WAE’EESAAA AN AAQEEMOOA DEENA WA LAA TATAFARRAQOOA FEEH KABURA A’LAL MUSHREKEEN MAA TADU’OOHUM ELAYHE ALLAAHO YAJTABEAA ELAYHE MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE ELAYHE MAN YYUNEEBU.\nHe hath prescribed for you the religion what He ordained unto Noah and that which revealed We unto thee and what ordained We unto Abraham and Moses and Jesus, that: “Establish ye the religion and be ye not divided therein;” Hard is it to the disbelievers what thou callest them unto; God chooseth unto Himself whomsoever He willeth, and guideth He unto Himself whosoever turneth - (to Him).\nوَمَا تَفَرَّقُوْۤا اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُ بَغْيًاۢ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ وَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى لَّقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ وَ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْرِثُوا الْكِتٰبَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهُ مُرِيْبٍ‏(14)\nWA MAA TAFARRAQOOA ILLAA MIN BA’DE MAA JAAA-AHOMUL I’LMO BAGHYAN BAYNAHUM WA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIN RABBEKA ELAA ELAA AJALIM LLAQUZEAAA BAYNAHUM WA INNAL LAZEENA AOORESOOA KETAABA MIN BA’DEHIM LAFEE SHAKKIM MINHO MOREEB.\nNor were they divided until after had come unto them the knowledge, out of rivalry between themselves; and had not the word gone forth from thy Lord (respiting them) to a fixed time, certainly, the affair had been decided between them; and verily, those who were made the heirs to the Book after them are certainly in disquieting doubt about it.\nفَلِذٰلِكَ فَادْعُ‌ ۚ وَاسْتَقِمْ كَمَاۤ اُمِرْتَ‌ۚ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‌ۚ وَقُلْ اٰمَنْتُ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ كِتٰبٍ‌‌ۚ وَاُمِرْتُ لِاَعْدِلَ بَيْنَكُمُ‌ؕ اَللّٰهُ رَبُّنَا وَرَبُّكُمْ‌ؕ لَنَاۤ اَعْمَالُنَا وَلَكُمْ اَعْمَالُكُمْ‌ۚ لَا حُجَّةَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمُ‌ؕ اَللّٰهُ يَجْمَعُ بَيْنَنَا‌ۚ وَاِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُؕ‏(15)\nFALEZAALEKA FAD-O’ WAASTAQEM KAMAA AUMERTA WA LAA TATTABEA’ AHWAAA-AHUM WA QUL AAMANTO BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO MIN KETAABIM WA AN A-A’BODA LEAAA’DELA BAYNAKUMU ALLAAHO RABBONAA WARABBUKUM LANAA A-A’MAALONAA WA LAKUM A-A’MAALOKUM LAA HUJJATA BAYNANAA WABAYNAKUMU ALLAAHO YAJMAU’U BAYNANAA WA ELAYHE AL-MASEERU.\nFor this then invite on thou (unto the truth) and be thou steadfast (on the right way) as thou art commanded; and follow thou not their vain desires, and say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Believe I in what God hath sent down of the Book; and I have been commanded to do justice between you; God is our Lord and your Lord; For us (is the responsibility) of our deeds, and for you (that of) your deeds; No contention (need there be) between us and you; God will gather us together; and unto Him is the ultimate return.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُحَآجُّوْنَ فِى اللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا اسْتُجِيْبَ لَهٗ حُجَّتُهُمْ دَاحِضَةٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَعَلَيْهِمْ غَضَبٌ وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌ‏(16)\nWAL LAZEENA YUHAAJJOONA FIL LAAHE MIN BA’DE MAA ASTUJEEBA LAHU HUJJATUHUM DAAHEZATUN I’NDAL RABBEHIM WA A’LAYHIM GHAZABUN WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN.\nAnd those who dispute about God after response made unto Him, their argument is vain unto their Lord, and upon them is the wrath, and for them is a severe chastisement.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ وَالْمِيْزَانَ‌ؕ وَمَا يُدْرِيْكَ لَعَلَّ السَّاعَةَ قَرِيْبٌ‏(17)\nALLAAHO LAZEE ANZALAL KETAABA BIL-HAQQE WAL MEEZAANA WA MAA YUDREEKA LA-A’LLAS SAA-A’TA QAREEB.\nGod is He Who sent down the Book with truth and the Balance, and what dost thou know? happly the Hour (of Reckoning) be nigh\nيَسْتَعْجِلُ بِهَا الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهَا‌ ۚ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مُشْفِقُوْنَ مِنْهَا ۙ وَيَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّهَا الْحَقُّ ‌ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُمَارُوْنَ فِى السَّاعَةِ لَفِىْ ضَلٰلٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(18)\nYASTAA’JELU BEHAA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BEHAA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MUSHFEQOONA MINHAA WA YA’LAMOON AANNAHAA HAQQO ALAA INNAL LAZEENA YUMAAROONA FIL AS-SAAA’ATE LAFEE ZALAALIM BA-E’ED.\nHasten it on (in challenge) they who believe not in it, and those who believe are afraid of it, and know they that it is the truth; Beware! Verily those who dispute about the Hour (of Reckoning) are far astray.\nاَللّٰهُ لَطِيْفٌۢ بِعِبَادِهٖ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ۚ وَهُوَ الْقَوِىُّ الْعَزِيْزُ‏(19)\nALLAAHO LATEEFUN BE-E’BAADEHI YARZOQO MAN YASHAAA-O WA HOWA QAWIYYUL A’ZEEZUL.\nGod is Benign unto His servants; Provideth He sustenance to whomsoever He willeth; and He is the All-Strong, the All-Mighty.\nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ حَرْثَ الْاٰخِرَةِ نَزِدْ لَهٗ فِىْ حَرْثِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ حَرْثَ الدُّنْيَا نُؤْتِهٖ مِنْهَا وَمَا لَهٗ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ مِنْ نَّصِيْبٍ‏(20)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDO HARSA AAKHERATE NAZED LAHU FEE HARSEH WA MAN KAANA YOREEDO HARSA DUNYAA NUTEH MINHAA WA MAA LAHU FIL AAKHERATE MIN NNASEEBIN.\nWhosoever intendeth the tilth of the hereafter, We increase for him in his tilth; whosoever intended the tilth of this world, We give him of it, and for him in the hereafter shall not be any share.\nاَمْ لَهُمْ شُرَكٰٓؤُا شَرَعُوْا لَهُمْ مِّنَ الدِّيْنِ مَا لَمْ يَاْذَنْۢ بِهِ اللّٰهُ‌ؕ وَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةُ الْفَصْلِ لَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ وَاِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(21)\nAM LAHUM SHURAKAAAUA SHARAU’OOA LAHUM MENAL DEENE MAA LAM YAAZAN BEHIL LAAH WA LAWLAA KALEMATU FASLE LAQOZEYA BAYNAHUM WA INNA ZAALEMEEN LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nOr for them are any partners (of God) who have prescribed for them any religion which God doth not sanction? And had it not been for the word of decision (to wait until the Day of Reckoning), the decision would certainly have been made between them; and verily the unjust, for them shall be a painful chastisement.\nتَرَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ مُشْفِقِيْنَ مِمَّا كَسَبُوْا وَهُوَ وَاقِعٌۢ بِهِمْ‌ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فِىْ رَوْضَاتِ الْجَنّٰتِ‌ۚ لَهُمْ مَّا يَشَآءُوْنَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَضْلُ الْكَبِيْرُ‏(22)\nTARAL ZAALEMEEN MUSHFEQEENA MIMMAA KASABOO WA HOWA WAAQEA’UN BEHIM WA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FEE RAWZAATE AL-JANNAATE LAHUM MAA YASHAAOONA I’NDAL RABBEHIM ZAALEKA HOWA FAZLUL AL-KABEERU.\n(On that Day) thou wilt see the unjust alarmed for what they have earned, and (the chastisement for) it shall befall them; And those who believe and do good deeds shall be in the meadows of the Garden (of Paradise); For them shall be whatever they please with their Lord; that is the greatest grace.\nذٰ لِكَ الَّذِىْ يُبَشِّرُ اللّٰهُ عِبَادَهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ‌ؕ قُلْ لَّاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ اَجْرًا اِلَّا الْمَوَدَّةَ فِى الْقُرْبٰى‌ؕ وَمَنْ يَّقْتَرِفْ حَسَنَةً نَّزِدْ لَهٗ فِيْهَا حُسْنًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ شَكُوْرٌ‏(23)\nZAA LEKA LAZEE YUBASSHERU LAAHO E’EBAADAHU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS AS-SAALEHAATE QUL LAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE AJRAN ILLAA AL-MAWADDATA FIL AL-QURBAA WA MAN YYAQTAREF HASANATANW NNAZED LAHU FEEHAA HUSNANW INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR SHAKOORUN.\nThat is of which giveth God the glad tidings unto His servants who believe and do good deeds; Say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “I demand not of you any recompense for it (the toils of the apostleship) save the love of (my) relatives; and whosoever earneth good, We increase for him good therein, verily God is Oft-Forgiving, the Most Grateful (One).\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا‌ ۚ فَاِنْ يَّشَاِ اللّٰهُ يَخْتِمْ عَلٰى قَلْبِكَ‌ ؕ وَيَمْحُ اللّٰهُ الْبَاطِلَ وَيُحِقُّ الْحَقَّ بِكَلِمٰتِهٖۤ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(24)\nAM YAQOOLOONA TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN FA-IN YYASHAA LAAHO YAKHTEM A’LAA QALBEKA WAYAMHU LAAHO AL-BAATELA WAYUHEQQU HAQQA BEKALEMAATEH INNAHU A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nOr do they say: “He hath forged a lie against God?” But if God hath willed, He would have sealed thy heart (and quiet thee) and (yet) He would blot out the falsehood and prove the truth with His words; Verily He knoweth best whatever is in the breasts (hearts)\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يَقْبَلُ التَّوْبَةَ عَنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَعْفُوْا عَنِ السَّيِّاٰتِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ ۙ‏(25)\nWA HOWA LAZEE YAQBALU AT-TAWBATA A’N E’BAADEHI WAYAA’FOOA A’NIL SAYYE-AATE YA’LAMO MAA TAF-A’LOON.\nHe it is Who accepteth repentance from His servants, and forgiveth the sins, and knoweth He whatever ye do,\nوَيَسْتَجِيْبُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَيَزِيْدُهُمْ مِّنْ فَضْلِهٖ‌ؕ وَالْكٰفِرُوْنَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌ‏(26)\nWAYASTAJEEBU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WAYAZEEDUHUM MIN FAZLEH KAAFEROONA LAHUM A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN.\nAnd He respondeth to those who believe and do good deeds, and increaseth unto them of His grace; And the disbelievers, for them shall be a severe chastisement.\nوَلَوْ بَسَطَ اللّٰهُ الرِّزْقَ لِعِبَادِهٖ لَبَغَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلٰكِنْ يُّنَزِّلُ بِقَدَرٍ مَّا يَشَآءُ ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِعِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرٌۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(27)\nWA LAW BASATA LAAHO RIZQA LE-E’BAADEHI LABAGHAWA FIL ARZE WA LAAKIL YYUNAZZELU BEQADARIN MAA YASHAAA INNAHU BE-E’BAADEHI KHABEERUM BASEER.\nAnd should God amplify the sustenance unto His servants, they would certainly rebel in the earth, but He sendeth it down by measure as He willeth; Verily of His servants, He is All-Aware, All-Seeing.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُنَزِّلُ الْغَيْثَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا قَنَطُوْا وَيَنْشُرُ رَحْمَتَهٗ‌ ؕ وَهُوَ الْوَلِىُّ الْحَمِيْدُ‏(28)\nWA HOWA LAZEE YUNAZZELU AL-GHAYSA MIN BA’DE MAA QANATOOA WAYANSHURU RAHMATAH WA HOWA AL-WALEAAAU AL-HAMEEDU.\nHe it is Who sendeth down the rain after what they have despaired, and spreadeth His Mercy; And He is the (Greatest) Guardian, the (Most) Praised One.\nوَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِهٖ خَلْقُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَثَّ فِيْهِمَا مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ‌ ؕ وَهُوَ عَلٰى جَمْعِهِمْ اِذَا يَشَآءُ قَدِيْرٌ‏(29)\nWA MIN AAYAATEHI KHALQUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BASSA FEEHEMAA MIN DAAAB-BATIL WA HOWA A’LAA JAME’EHEM EZAA YASHAAA QADEER.\nAnd of His signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth and (the creation of) what He hath spread out in both of them of the animate beings and for their gathering together when He willeth, He is All-Powerful.\nوَمَاۤ اَصَابَكُمْ مِّنْ مُّصِيْبَةٍ فَبِمَا كَسَبَتْ اَيْدِيْكُمْ وَيَعْفُوْا عَنْ كَثِيْرٍؕ‏(30)\nWA MAA AASAABAKUM MIN MMUSEEBATIN FA BEMAA KASABAT AYDEEKUM WAYAA’FOOA A’N KASEERIN.\nAnd whatever befalleth you of a misfortune, it is what your (own) hands have wrought, and (yet) He pardoneth the most of your sins.\nوَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ ۖۚ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(31)\nWA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA FIL ARZE WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nYe can not frustrate (God's) will in the earth, and for you (there) is none other than God, Guardian or a Helper.\nوَمِنْ اٰيٰتِهِ الْجَوَارِ فِى الْبَحْرِ كَالْاَعْلَامِؕ‏(32)\nWA MIN AAAYAATEHE JAWAARIL FIL BAHRE KAALAAA’LAAME.\nAnd among His signs are the ships in the sea like mountains.\nاِنْ يَّشَاْ يُسْكِنِ الرِّيْحَ فَيَظْلَلْنَ رَوَاكِدَ عَلٰى ظَهْرِهٖؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍ شَكُوْرٍۙ‏(33)\nIN YYASHAA YUSKENE AR-REEHA FAYAZLALNA RAWAAKEDA A’LAA ZAHREH INNAL FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEKULLE SABBAARIN SHAKOORIN.\nIf He willeth, He lulleth the wind that they (the ships) lie motionless on the back of it (the sea); Verily in this are signs for every steadfast grateful one,\nاَوْ يُوْبِقْهُنَّ بِمَا كَسَبُوْا وَيَعْفُ عَنْ كَثِيْرٍ‏(34)\nAW YOOBEQHUNNA BEMAA KASABOO WAYAA’FU A’N KASEERIM.\nOr He may cause them to perish for what they have wrought, and (yet) He pardoneth the most,\nوَّيَعْلَمَ الَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا ؕ مَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ مَّحِيْصٍ‏(35)\nWWAYAA’LAMA LAZEENA YUJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATENAA MAA LAHUM MIN MAHEES.\nAnd (that) may know those who dispute about Our signs; For them (there) is no refuge.\nفَمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَمَتَاعُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا‌ۚ وَمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَۚ‏(36)\nFAMAA MAA OOTEETUM MIN SHAY-IN FAMATAAUL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA MAA I’NDAL LAAHE KHAYRUL KHAYRUWN LILLAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’LAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\nAnd whatever ye are given (here) is but a provision for the life of this world, and what is with God is better and more lasting for those who believe and on their Lord they rely;\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَجْتَنِبُوْنَ كَبٰٓئِرَ الْاِثْمِ وَالْفَوَاحِشَ وَاِذَا مَا غَضِبُوْا هُمْ يَغْفِرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(37)\nWAL LAZEENA YAJTANEBOONA KABAAAERA AL-AESME WAL FAWAAHESHA WA EZAA MAA GHAZEBOOA HUM YAGHFEROONA.\nAnd those who shun the great sins and filthiness, and when they are angry, they forgive;\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اسْتَجَابُوا لِرَبِّهِمْ وَاَقَامُوْا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاَمْرُهُمْ شُوْرٰى بَيْنَهُمْ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(38)\nWAL LAZEENA ASTAJAABOOA LE-RABBEHIM WAAQAAMOOA SALAATA WAAMRUHUM SHOORAA BAYNAHUM WA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOONA.\nAnd those who respond to their Lord, and establish prayer, and (conduct) their affairs with counsel among themselves, what We have provided them with their sustenance they spend,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اِذَاۤ اَصَابَهُمُ الْبَغْىُ هُمْ يَنْتَصِرُوْنَ‏(39)\nWAL LAZEENA EZAA AASAABAHUMU AL-BAGHAAU HUM YANTASEROONA.\nAnd (those) who when afflicteth them any great wrong, they get helped by themselves.\nوَجَزٰٓؤُا سَيِّئَةٍ سَيِّئَةٌ مِّثْلُهَا‌ۚ فَمَنْ عَفَا وَاَصْلَحَ فَاَجْرُهٗ عَلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(40)\nWAJAZAAAUA SAYATIN SAYYE-ATUM MMESLUHAA FAMAN A’AFAA WAASLAHA FA AJROHU A’LAL LAAH INNAHU LAA YOHIBBUL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd the recompense for an evil shall be an ill-return like unto it, but (if) one pardoneth and amendeth, his reward is incumbent on God; Verily He loveth not the unjust.\nوَلَمَنِ انْتَصَرَ بَعْدَ ظُلْمِهٖ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ مَا عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ سَبِيْلٍؕ‏(41)\nWA LAMANISH ANTASARA BA’DA ZULMEH FA-OOLAAA-EKA MAA A’LAYHIM MIN SABEELIN.\nAnd whosoever defendeth himself (in avenging) after being oppressed, then against these there is no way (to blame)\nاِنَّمَا السَّبِيْلُ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَظْلِمُوْنَ النَّاسَ وَ يَبْغُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ‌ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(42)\nINNAMAA AS-SABEELU A’LAL LAZEENA YAZLEMOON NAASA WA YABGHOONA FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQ OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nThe way (to blame) is against those who do injustice unto the people and transgress in the earth unjustly; these, for them shall be a painful chastisement.\nوَلَمَنْ صَبَرَ وَغَفَرَ اِنَّ ذٰلِكَ لَمِنْ عَزْمِ الْاُمُوْرِ‏(43)\nWALAMAN SABARA WAGHAFARA INNAL ZAALEKA LAMEN A’AZME AL-AUMOORE.\nAnd indeed whosoever remaineth patient and forgiveth, verily this is an act of great resolution.\nوَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ‌ ؕ وَتَرَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ لَمَّا رَاَوُا الْعَذَابَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ هَلْ اِلٰى مَرَدٍّ مِّنْ سَبِيْلٍ‌ۚ‏(44)\nWA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN WALIYYINW MIN BA’DEHI WA TARAL ZAALEMEEN LAMMAA RAAWUA A’ZAABA YAQOOLOONA HAL ELAA MARADDIN MIN SABEELIN.\nAnd whomsoever God alloweth to stray, for him (there) shall not be any guardian after it; and thou shalt behold the unjust when they see the chastisement, saying: “Is there any way (to help us) to return\nوَتَرٰٮهُمْ يُعْرَضُوْنَ عَلَيْهَا خٰشِعِيْنَ مِنَ الذُّلِّ يَنْظُرُوْنَ مِنْ طَرْفٍ خَفِىٍّ‌ ؕ وَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَاَهْلِيْهِمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ فِىْ عَذَابٍ مُّقِيْمٍ‏(45)\nWA TARAAHUM YUA’RAZOONA A’LAYHAA KHAASHEE’EENA MENAL AZ-ZULLE YANZOROONA MIN TARFIN KHAFEAAAIN WA QAALA LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAL KHAASEREEN LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM WA AHLEEHIM YAWMA QEYAAMATE ALAA INNAL ZAALEMEEN FEE A’ZAABIN MMUQEEMIN.\nAnd thou shalt see them brought unto it humbled of disgrace, looking with a stealthy glance; And shall say those who believe: “Verily the losers are those who lost their selves and their people on the Day of Reckoning.” Beware! verily the unjust shall be in a lasting chastisement.\nوَمَا كَانَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ يَنْصُرُوْنَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ سَبِيْلٍؕ‏(46)\nWA MAA KAANA LAHUM MIN AAWLEEAAAA YANSOROONAHUM MIN DOONIL LAAH WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN SABEELIN.\nAnd there shall not be for them any of the guardians to help them besides God; and whomsoever God alloweth to stray, for him shall not be any (other) way (of being guided aright)\nاِسْتَجِيْبُوْا لِرَبِّكُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ يَوْمٌ لَّا مَرَدَّ لَهٗ مِنَ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ مَّلْجَاٍ يَّوْمَئِذٍ وَّمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّكِيْرٍ‏(47)\nAESTAJEEBOOA LERABBEKUM MIN QABLE AN YAATEYA YAWMUL LAA MARADDA LAHU MENAL LAAH MAA LAKUM MIN MMALJAA YAWMA-EZIN WA MAA LAKUM MIN NNAKEERIN.\nRespond ye unto your Lord ere cometh the Day from God for which there is no averting; for you shall not be any refuge on the Day, and nor for you will it be to make any denial.\nفَاِنْ اَعْرَضُوْا فَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَفِيْظًا‌ؕ اِنْ عَلَيْكَ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّاۤ اِذَاۤ اَذَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنَّا رَحْمَةً فَرِحَ بِهَا‌ۚ وَاِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ سَيِّئَةٌۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ فَاِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ كَفُوْرٌ‏(48)\nFA-IN A-A’RAZOO FAMAA ARSALNAAKA A’LAYHIM HAFEEZAN IN A’LAYKA ILLAA BALAAGHUL WA INNAA EZAA AZAQNAN INSAANA MINNAA RAHMATAM FAREHA BEHAA WA IN TOSIBHUM SAYYE-ATUM BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEHIM FA-INNAL INSAANA KAFOORUN.\nAnd if they turn away, then We have not sent thee over them as a watcher; On thee is naught but only to convey (Our Word unto mankind); And verily when We make man taste mercy from Us, rejoiceth he thereby, and if afflicteth them any ill for what have done their (own) hands, then verily man (forgetteth all Our grace and) turneth ingrate.\nلِّلَّهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ‌ؕ يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ‌ ؕ يَهَبُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ اِنَاثًا وَّيَهَبُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ الذُّكُوْرَ ۙ‏(49)\nLILLAAH MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAAA YAHABU LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O AENAASAN WWAYAHABU LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O AZ-ZUKOORA.\nGod’s is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; Createth He whatever He willeth; Granteth He unto whomsoever He willeth females and granteth He whomsoever He willeth males,\nاَوْ يُزَوِّجُهُمْ ذُكْرَانًا وَّاِنَاثًا‌ ۚ وَيَجْعَلُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ عَقِيْمًا‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌ قَدِيْرٌ‏(50)\nAW YUZAWJUHUM ZUKRAANAN WWAANAASAN WAYAJA’ALU MAN YASHAAA-O A’AQEEMAN INNAHU A’LEEM QADEER.\nOr mingleth them of both males (i.e., sons) and females (i.e., daughters), and maketh whomsoever He willeth barren; Verily He is the All-Knowing, the All-Powerful.\nوَمَا كَانَ لِبَشَرٍ اَنْ يُّكَلِّمَهُ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا وَحْيًا اَوْ مِنْ وَّرَآىٴِ حِجَابٍ اَوْ يُرْسِلَ رَسُوْلًا فَيُوْحِىَ بِاِذْنِهٖ مَا يَشَآءُ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِىٌّ حَكِيْمٌ‏(51)\nWA MAA KAANA LEBASHARIN AN YYUKALLEMAHU LAAHO ILLAA WAHYAN AW MIN WWARAAAA MINW AW YURSELA RASOOLAM FAYOOHEAAA BE-IZNEH MAA YASHAAU INNAHU A’ALEAAAUN HAKEEM.\nAnd it is not for any man that God should speak unto him save by revelation or from behind a veil, or by sending a messenger and to reveal by His permission what He willeth; Verily He is the Most High, the All-Wise.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ رُوْحًا مِّنْ اَمْرِنَا‌ ؕ مَا كُنْتَ تَدْرِىْ مَا الْكِتٰبُ وَلَا الْاِيْمَانُ وَلٰكِنْ جَعَلْنٰهُ نُوْرًا نَّهْدِىْ بِهٖ مَنْ نَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا‌ ؕ وَاِنَّكَ لَتَهْدِىْۤ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍۙ‏(52)\nWA KAZAALEKA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA ROOHAN MIN AAMRENAA MAA KUNTA LAA MAA KETAABO WA LAA AL-AEEMAANU WA LAAKIL LAW NOORAN NNAHDEAA BEHI MAN NNASHAAU MIN E’EBAADENAA WA LATAHDEAA ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nThus did We reveal unto thee Our guidance by Our command; Thou didst know not what the Book (Qur'an) was, nor the faith, but We made it a light, guide We thereby whomsoever We will of Our servants; and verily guideth thou unto the Right Path;\nصِرَاطِ اللّٰهِ الَّذِىْ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اَلَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ تَصِيْرُ الْاُمُوْرُ‏(53)\nSERAATE LAAHE LAZEE LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ ALAA ELAL LAAHE TASEERU OMOOR.\nThe path of God, Whose is whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth; Be it known! Unto God (alone) shall be referred all affairs.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Shooraa (The Council)\nThis Surah has 53 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will be from among those people on whom the angels send salutations and pray for their forgiveness.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites this Surah will be raised on the Day of Reckoning with a face as bright as the full moon and he will be told: ‘You are from those who used to recite Surah Shooraa. If you knew the reward for this, you would never have felt tired of reciting it.’ The angels will then be ordered to take him to Paradise where he will find a palace made of red rubies. There will be two huries and a thousand slaves in that palace.\nIf this Surah is written and kept as a talisman, it becomes a means of protection and drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved is especially good for those intending to travel as it provides for a journey without unforeseen problems."
